# chesscito-landing (www.chesscito.com) — environment template
#
# NAMES ONLY. Never commit a value to this file. Real values live in the
# Vercel project `chesscito-landing` and, for local runs, in `.env.local`
# (gitignored).
#
# Mirrors the per-app convention already used by apps/web/.env.template.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — read-only access to the eight `stats_*` aggregation RPCs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added in Phase B of docs/plans/2026-08-04-stats-consolidation-execution-plan.md.
# These are the FIRST secrets this project has ever had; the rules below are
# what keep that fact cheap to live with.
#
#   - SERVER-ONLY. Read exclusively from src/lib/supabase/server.ts, which
#     starts with `import "server-only"` — a client-component import is a
#     build error, not a runtime surprise.
#   - NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_` PREFIX, ever. A prefixed name is inlined into the
#     browser bundle at build time; that is how a service role key leaks.
#     Guarded by src/lib/supabase/__tests__/secret-isolation.test.ts.
#   - Required in BOTH `production` and `preview` of the Vercel project
#     `chesscito-landing`. Server variables are not baked into the client
#     bundle, so they need no redeploy to change — but the code that reads
#     them does need one deploy to ship.
#   - DO NOT copy these into apps/web: that app already declares its own
#     SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Two projects, two entries,
#     same database.
#   - Missing or empty → getSupabaseServer() returns null, the aggregator
#     degrades to em-dashes, and the page still renders. Deleting the two
#     variables is a complete rollback.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /stats cache invalidation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added in Phase E. Shared secret for POST /api/revalidate-stats, which flushes
# the "public-stats" tag.
#
#   - SERVER-ONLY, no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix. A prefixed name is inlined into
#     the browser bundle, which would publish the key that lets anyone flush
#     the cache at will.
#   - The endpoint FAILS CLOSED: with this variable unset or empty it answers
#     401 to every request, including one carrying the right value by luck.
#     An unconfigured secret must not become an open door.
#   - ⚠️ This endpoint exists because a DEPLOY DOES NOT PURGE Next's Data
#     Cache. A broken census once survived 18 h 34 min and a full deploy, so
#     "just redeploy" is not an invalidation strategy.
#   - NOT loaded in Vercel yet — deliberately. Until it is, /stats can only be
#     refreshed by waiting out the 900 s TTL.

STATS_REVALIDATE_TOKEN=
